This is a great idea except for one thing: it's stupid.  You have three
choices: either make every player in the game take their turn before
anyone can move, or have a ticker like in a MUD, or allow anyone to 
move at any time (as you can now).  The first would slow the game
to a crawl (but keep the game reasonably similar), the second would
turn it into a pretty lame MUD, and the third would turn it into a 
really lame version of Hunt.

How do you stop a level 20 character with a +8 Stormbringer from sitting
around the level 1 steps waiting for new characters and killing them
in one blow?  Great tactic, he'd get all kinds of healing potions, 
a tinning kit, the occasional magic marker, rings and wands, etc.  

Also, do you have just one dungeon?  Wouldn't that get boring once you
knew it?  If each dungeon is random, how do the players ever interact?
And don't even *think* about being able to find food in a dungeon
with 10 or 20 players.

If you want to play MUD, play MUD.  Nethack is a single-user game.
